---
/* What an archive stands on, grouped and ranked.

   All eight archives had a sources page and no two shared a line — 1,277
   lines of it. But the disagreement is not what it looks like. They are not
   eight renderings of one idea; they are using FOUR DIFFERENT AXES:

     Blazevic    `weight`  — evidential authority. state / register / tree /
                 background / rejected / absent, in the order it trusts them.
     Lerena      `tier`    — PRIMARY / SECONDARY / REFERENCE.
     Falco       `g`       — record type and country. Parish registers, Civil
                 registration, Newspapers (Australia), Catalogue (UK).
     Defranceski `kind`    — format. Publication, Archive, Portal, Database.
     Mazza and Booyzen group by narrative instead: "Tried and found wanting",
                 "The Transvaal, before anyone thought this family was there".

   NONE OF THOSE IS WRONG AND THIS FILE IMPOSES NONE OF THEM. An archive that
   ranks by authority is making a different argument from one that sorts by
   record type, and flattening the two would lose the argument to make a table
   look tidy. What every one of them actually does is the same: GROUPED ROWS,
   IN AN ORDER THE ARCHIVE CHOSE, each row a source with a description and
   somewhere to go. That is what is shared, and it is all that is shared.

   Blazevic's page states the thesis better than this comment can, so it is
   quoted rather than paraphrased: «a sources page that prints them as four
   paragraphs of similar length is quietly saying they are not four different
   kinds of thing». The group label and its position carry that, so both are
   the archive's to set and neither is defaulted here.

     groups  [{ label, note, rows }] — rendered in the order given, which is
             the order the archive trusts them. `note` is the one-line gloss
             under the label: Blazevic's weights table, Mazza's "not seen
             here", Lerena's tier definition.
     rows    [{ title, what, holder, kind, carries, caution, volumes,
                href, hrefLabel, tag, cite }]
             Only `title` is required. `holder` and `kind` render as a small
             key/value pair; `caution` as a note; `volumes` as a plain list;
             `tag` as a chip against the title, for a per-row qualifier that
             is not the group — Lerena's "full-text transcript read" belongs
             there rather than concatenated into its tier, which is why that
             archive has 26 distinct tiers for 3 tiers.
     u       the archive's url helper. Hand-written HTML in source data is
             common here, and an href='/x' in it needs the site base — the
             trap /open-questions/ and /corrections/ both fell into.
     html    true when the data carries markup. Default true, because six of
             the eight hold HTML in these fields already.
*/
const { groups = [], u = (p) => p, html = true } = Astro.props;

/* Prefix the site base onto hrefs written into the data by hand. */
const B = u("/");
const fix = (s) => String(s ?? "").replace(/href=(['"])\//g, `href=$1${B}`);
const F = (s) => (html ? fix(s) : String(s ?? ""));
---
<div class="sr">
  {groups.map((g) => (
    <section class="sr-g">
      {g.label && (
        <div class="sr-lab">
          {g.label}{g.note ? <span class="sr-note"> — <Fragment set:html={F(g.note)} /></span> : null}
        </div>
      )}
      {(g.rows || []).map((r) => (
        <article class="sr-row">
          <h3 class="sr-t">
            {r.href ? <a href={u(r.href)}><Fragment set:html={F(r.title)} /></a>
                    : <Fragment set:html={F(r.title)} />}
            {r.tag ? <span class="sr-tag">{r.tag}</span> : null}
          </h3>
          {(r.holder || r.kind) && (
            <table class="sr-kv"><tbody>
              {r.holder && <tr><th>Held by</th><td set:html={F(r.holder)} /></tr>}
              {r.kind && <tr><th>What it is</th><td set:html={F(r.kind)} /></tr>}
            </tbody></table>
          )}
          {r.what && <p class="sr-w" set:html={F(r.what)} />}
          {(r.volumes || []).length > 0 && (
            <ul class="sr-vol">{r.volumes.map((v) => <li set:html={F(v)} />)}</ul>
          )}
          {r.carries && <p class="sr-c" set:html={F(r.carries)} />}
          {r.caution && <div class="sr-caution" set:html={F(r.caution)} />}
          {r.cite && <p class="sr-cite mono" set:html={F(r.cite)} />}
          {r.href && r.hrefLabel && (
            <p class="sr-go"><a href={u(r.href)}>{r.hrefLabel}</a></p>
          )}
        </article>
      ))}
    </section>
  ))}
</div>

<style is:global>
  .sr-g { margin: 0 0 1.8rem; }
  .sr-lab {
    font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .13em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3); margin: 0 0 .5rem;
  }
  .sr-note { text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; font-weight: 400; }
  .sr-row { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: .9rem 0 .35rem; }
  .sr-g .sr-row:first-of-type { border-top: 0; padding-top: .1rem; }
  .sr-t { margin: 0 0 .45rem; font-size: 1.02rem; font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 600; }
  .sr-tag {
    margin-left: .5rem; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 9.5px; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); padding: 1px 5px; white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .sr-kv { margin: 0 0 .6rem; border-collapse: collapse; }
  .sr-kv th {
    white-space: nowrap; text-align: left; padding: 0 .8rem .15rem 0; vertical-align: top;
    font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 9.5px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .11em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .sr-kv td { padding: 0 0 .15rem; font-size: 14px; }
  .sr-w, .sr-c { margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  .sr-c { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .sr-vol { margin: 0 0 .5rem; padding-left: 1.1em; }
  .sr-vol li { margin-bottom: .2rem; }
  .sr-caution {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--ochre); padding: .4rem 0 .4rem .7rem;
    margin: 0 0 .5rem; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 14.5px;
  }
  .sr-cite { font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-3); margin: 0 0 .4rem; }
  .sr-go { margin: 0 0 .2rem; font-size: 14px; }
</style>
